---
description: When and how to delegate repo work to a Cursor cloud agent, and how to accept it
alwaysApply: false
---
# Cloud agents
- Delegate code or analysis that reads/changes many files or needs build/test loops (brief ~10-20 lines). Do it yourself for a few lines, one file, or work needing server, secrets or chat history. Never both.
- Launch: check no branch/PR/agent exists for the issue; one issue, one agent; branch `<role>/<NN>-<slug>`; attach this repo's rules (they are in `.cursor/`, the agent reads them); prompt in English: issue number, goal, acceptance criteria, known context, out of scope, branch. Remind it: PR sections without «Учебный кейс»; no agent/bot/tool names in commits, PR or issue text.
- Prefer the cheaper pool for routine code and repo-reading analysis/review; follow the current usage mode if the project sets one.
- Model: default Grok, medium effort (low mechanical, high multi-file/auth/security, xhigh hard). Opus only if Grok xhigh failed or the task is big and critical; state why.
- Cloud agent rules: regular PR into `main`, never push to `main`, never merge, never edit wiki/board, no secrets or server access. In the PR «Задача» section link `#NN` only; never write `closes`/`fix`/`fixes`. Mark PR ready when CI is green. Final report (English): PR URL, head sha, what changed, tests added, open doubts.
- Acceptance: the launcher owns the result. Strip Cursor PR-body markers and the «Open in Cursor» footer (`gh pr edit --body-file`). Fixes via reply to the same agent. Then merge gates: CI + Cursor Automations + step 6 escalation (`project-cursor-automations.mdc`, `playbook-step-06-review.mdc`).
